---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Ravikumar Buragapu | Director of Engineering, AI Engineering and Reliability"
			description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section aria-labelledby="hero-title">
				<p class="kicker">AI ENGINEERING · PLATFORM ENGINEERING · RELIABILITY</p>

				<h1 id="hero-title">Engineering AI for the real world.</h1>

				<p class="lede">
					Director of Engineering at Oracle Health. I turn emerging AI
					into platforms that are secure, observable, and ready for
					production.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="impact-title">
				<h2 id="impact-title">Impact</h2>
				<ul class="proof">
					<li>
						<strong>10,000+ developers</strong>
						reached by the agentic engineering strategy I helped define at Wells Fargo
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Regulated scale</strong>
						leading infrastructure, reliability, and data intelligence engineering across commercial, regulated, and Federal platforms at Oracle Health
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>AI-driven service maturity</strong>
						built the Service Maturity Insights platform and led the Agentic AI Builders Group at Adobe
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>25+ years</strong>
						building enterprise platforms, from application development to AI engineering
					</li>
					{/* Add outcome numbers only when you can defend each one and your
					employer allows it. Format: metric, baseline, your role. Examples:
					<li><strong>Metric here</strong> what changed, where, and your role</li>
					<li><strong>10 PB, 500M+ records</strong> on the Oracle Health data platforms I lead</li>
					*/}
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="intro-title">
				<h2 id="intro-title" class="visually-hidden">Introduction</h2>
				<p>
					I’m Ravikumar Buragapu, a Director of Engineering at Oracle
					Health, focused on AI engineering, platform engineering, and
					reliability at enterprise scale. I work on turning emerging
					technologies—from GenAI to agentic systems—into platforms that
					are secure, observable, resilient, and ready for production.
				</p>

				<p>
					My perspective is simple: the next phase of AI will be shaped
					not just by what models can do, but by how we engineer the
					systems around them—identity, evaluation, permissions,
					infrastructure, operational controls, and human accountability.
				</p>

				<p>
					<a href="/writing">Read my writing</a>
					·
					<a href="/projects">See my projects</a>
					·
					<a href="/speak">Speaking</a>
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="focus-title">
				<h2 id="focus-title">What I focus on</h2>

				<h3>AI and agentic systems</h3>
				<p>
					Designing the engineering foundations for production AI:
					agent identity, least-privilege access, evaluation,
					guardrails, observability, and controlled autonomy. I believe
					autonomy should be earned through measurable evidence and
					backed by explicit operational controls.
				</p>

				<h3>Platform engineering and developer productivity</h3>
				<p>
					Building platforms, reusable engineering capabilities,
					and automation that help teams deliver software faster
					while maintaining security, consistency, and quality. The
					goal is less friction for engineers without giving up
					consistency or control.
				</p>

				<h3>Reliability and operational intelligence</h3>
				<p>
					Engineering resilient, data-intensive systems through
					observability, SRE practices, incident automation,
					capacity engineering, and measurable service objectives,
					so architectural decisions connect to measurable outcomes.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="projects-title">
				<h2 id="projects-title">Featured projects</h2>
				<p>
					Open-source work on measuring and controlling AI systems in
					practice.
				</p>

				<div class="cards">
					<article class="card">
						<p class="tag">OPEN-SOURCE TOOLKIT · PYTHON · DOCKER</p>
						<h3><a href="/projects/benchmarkkit">BenchmarkKit</a></h3>
						<p>
							Repeatable benchmarks for LLM inference servers and RAG
							pipelines: latency percentiles, throughput, cost,
							retrieval recall, and answer support.
						</p>
					</article>

					<article class="card">
						<p class="tag">RAG RESEARCH · EVALUATION</p>
						<h3><a href="/projects/rag-judge-eval">Validated RAG Eval Harness</a></h3>
						<p>
							Do LLM judges agree with human reviewers? A
							human-validated comparison of judge prompts on answer
							correctness and citation support, measured with
							Cohen’s kappa.
						</p>
					</article>

					<article class="card">
						<p class="tag">MULTI-AGENT · MCP · LANGGRAPH</p>
						<h3><a href="/projects/chief-of-staff">Personal Chief of Staff</a></h3>
						<p>
							A local-first, LangGraph-supervised assistant that uses
							read-only MCP servers for briefings, email triage, and
							meeting prep.
						</p>
					</article>

				</div>

				<p>
					<a href="/projects">All projects and research notes</a>
					— chunking, tokenizers, embeddings, sequence models, and
					vector search.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="experience-title">
				<h2 id="experience-title">Engineering leadership at scale</h2>

				<ul class="orgs">
					<li>
						<strong>Oracle Health</strong>
						<span class="sub">AI-native infrastructure and enterprise reliability</span>
						<p>
							I lead engineering across infrastructure, reliability,
							and data intelligence platforms serving commercial,
							regulated, and Federal environments.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Wells Fargo</strong>
						<span class="sub">Agentic AI and engineering transformation</span>
						<p>
							I formed the Agentic and GenAI Squad and helped shape
							agentic engineering strategy across an organization
							reaching more than 10,000 developers.
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Adobe</strong>
						<span class="sub">Platform engineering and developer experience</span>
						<p>
							I led platform engineering and the Agentic AI Builders
							Group, and built an AI-driven Service Maturity Insights
							platform.
						</p>
					</li>
				</ul>

				<p>
					Earlier roles include Kohl’s and Charles Schwab, building
					on a software engineering career that began in India in
					2000. Over 25 years that has spanned enterprise
					applications, data platforms, cloud infrastructure,
					developer productivity, and AI.
				</p>

				<p><a href="/about">More about my background and experience</a></p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="writing-title">
				<h2 id="writing-title">Ideas on engineering what comes next</h2>

				<p>
					I write about the engineering decisions that determine
					whether AI systems can be trusted in production—from
					evaluation and identity to governance, operational
					reliability, and the boundaries of agent autonomy.
				</p>

				<article>
					<h3>
						<a href="/blog/earning-agentic-autonomy">
							Earning Agentic Autonomy: An Eval Architecture for AI Agents
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p>
						How evaluation evidence, explicit controls, and
						runtime enforcement can help determine when an AI
						agent is ready to act with greater autonomy.
					</p>
				</article>

				<article>
					<h3>
						<a href="/blog/hard-part-of-agents">
							The Hard Part of Agents Isn’t the Model
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p>
						Why identity, permissions, review load, observability,
						and cost decide whether agents survive in production.
					</p>
				</article>

				<p><a href="/writing">Explore all articles</a></p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="speaking-title">
				<h2 id="speaking-title">Speaking</h2>
				<p>
					I speak about production AI, platform engineering,
					developer productivity, and reliability. Recent talks include
					DPE Summit 2023, ScyllaDB Summit 2023, and Percona
					Community Live 2022.
				</p>
				<p><a href="/speak">Talks, topics, and how to invite me</a></p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="connect-title">
				<h2 id="connect-title">Let’s exchange ideas</h2>

				<p>
					I’m interested in conversations about production AI,
					agentic architectures, platform engineering, reliability,
					and the future of engineering organizations.
				</p>

				<p>
					<a href="/about">About me</a>
					·
					<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ravikumar-buragapu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
					{/* When your domain email is ready, add:
					·
					<a href="mailto:contact@ravikumarburagapu.com">Email</a> */}
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.kicker,
	.tag {
		font-size: 0.8em;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
		margin-bottom: 0.5em;
	}
	.lede {
		font-size: 1.15em;
		max-width: 38em;
	}
	.proof {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
		list-style: none;
		padding: 1rem 0;
		margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		font-size: 0.95em;
	}
	.proof strong {
		display: block;
		font-size: 1.1em;
	}
	.cards {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin: 1.5rem 0;
	}
	.card {
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1rem;
	}
	.card h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5em 0;
	}
	.card p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
		font-size: 0.95em;
	}
	.orgs {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 1rem 0;
	}
	.orgs li {
		padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
		border-left: 3px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.orgs strong {
		display: block;
	}
	.orgs .sub {
		display: block;
		font-size: 0.85em;
		color: rgb(var(--gray));
	}
	.orgs p {
		margin: 0.35rem 0 0 0;
	}
	.visually-hidden {
		position: absolute;
		width: 1px;
		height: 1px;
		overflow: hidden;
		clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
</style>